    "module": {
      "title": "SNAP-style whole-dollar allotment (rounding fixture)",
      "summary": "A deliberately small, illustrative SNAP-style calculation used to exercise\nthe currency output-rounding contract (Phase-A A8) end to end in both the\nexplain and dense paths. Amounts and coefficients are illustrative, not the\nreal SNAP figures.\n\nnet_income rounds a whole-dollar figure (a no-op when already whole), and\nallotment both depends on the rounded net_income AND rounds its own output\nhalf-up to whole dollars — so the fixture covers a rounded rule feeding a\nsecond rounded rule, which is the composition the contract must preserve."
